#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198154 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b31f2bdc-c267-5fc7-bd0f-283777ee4fee" :knowledge-point/title "The Derivative of a Three-Component Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/id #uuid "a5637d71-22d4-548e-ad36-d09bff61d643" :question/math-academy-id "e-2398" :question/problem "Find the derivative of  $\\mathbf f(t) = \\langle \\sin t ,\\cos t , t \\rangle$ at $t= \\dfrac{\\pi}4.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $\\mathbf f'(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute $\\mathbf f'\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}4\\right),$ we substitute $t=\\dfrac{\\pi}4$ into the expression for $\\mathbf f'(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}),\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}),\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198157 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "072ad553-dd0b-58e0-b3e2-082c6d9866dd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/id #uuid "c737d317-8e09-5ccb-b816-b5f56e925ba9" :question/math-academy-id "e-609" :question/problem "Given that $\\mathbf r(t) = \\langle 10t^4 ,\\, 6\\ln t\\rangle,$ what is $\\mathbf r'\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)?$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t) = 10t^4,$ we have\n\n$$\nx'(t) = 40t^3,\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\nx'\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right) = 40\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)^3 = 5.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t) = 6 \\ln t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t)=\\frac{6}{t},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\ny'\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right) = \\dfrac{6}{\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)}=12.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2}) & =⟨{x}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2}),\\,{y}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,\\,12⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198158 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f0e2596-73d6-540c-af84-b19a943da6a8" :knowledge-point/title "The Second Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/id #uuid "cde8f304-4937-5eb7-a8e1-a08355ee4d4e" :question/math-academy-id "e-611" :question/problem "Given that $\\mathbf r(t) = \\langle t^6,\\, t^5\\rangle,$ Calculate $\\mathbf r''(t).$" :question/worked-solution "To find the second derivative of a vector-valued function, we find the second derivatives of the components.\n\n- For $x(t) = t^6,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =6{t}^{5} \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =30{t}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t) = t^5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =5{t}^{4} \\\\ {y}^{″}(t) & =20{t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨{x}^{″}(t),\\,{y}^{″}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨30{t}^{4},\\,20{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =10⟨3{t}^{4},\\,2{t}^{3}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326885 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f0e2596-73d6-540c-af84-b19a943da6a8" :knowledge-point/title "The Second Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e82bbec3-cbed-550a-b1a0-c09742375bcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{csc}⁡t({cot}^{2}⁡t+{csc}^{2}⁡t),\\,\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326887} {:answer/id #uuid "c21190ac-2d83-5bca-899e-b9665bee4e05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{cot}^{2}⁡t+{csc}^{2}⁡t,\\,-\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326888} {:answer/id #uuid "cea3a78c-710b-5714-99ad-af0c76a3d093" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{csc}⁡t(\\operatorname{cot}⁡t+\\operatorname{csc}⁡t),\\,\\frac{1}{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326889} {:answer/id #uuid "e74006aa-954a-54d4-8a08-3e7213a199b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{csc}⁡t({cot}^{2}⁡t+{csc}^{2}⁡t),\\,-\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326890} {:answer/id #uuid "06c9240a-0daa-563a-bde9-11b254179b0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{csc}⁡t(\\operatorname{cot}⁡t+\\operatorname{csc}⁡t),\\,\\frac{2}{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326891}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e74006aa-954a-54d4-8a08-3e7213a199b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{csc}⁡t({cot}^{2}⁡t+{csc}^{2}⁡t),\\,-\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326890} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf90a238-da1b-5802-8192-566872def271" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326886}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ea95f477-95b7-5171-a00b-e29976302120" :question/math-academy-id "q-123171" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{csc}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2})⟩,$ ${r}^{″}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the second derivative of a vector-valued function, we find the second derivatives of the components.\n\n- For $x(t)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t\\operatorname{csc}⁡t \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡t{cot}^{2}⁡t+{csc}^{3}⁡t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡t({cot}^{2}⁡t+{csc}^{2}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{2}{t} \\\\ {y}^{″}(t) & =-\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨{x}^{″}(t),\\,{y}^{″}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{csc}⁡t({cot}^{2}⁡t+{csc}^{2}⁡t),\\,-\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326892 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f0e2596-73d6-540c-af84-b19a943da6a8" :knowledge-point/title "The Second Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "120e0d02-39ff-52fe-acfa-b0536ce24c0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t)({tan}^{2}⁡(t)-{sec}^{2}⁡(2t)),\\,\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326894} {:answer/id #uuid "870bb444-8b25-5e47-bdcd-66ce10cd058a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t)({tan}^{2}⁡t+{sec}^{2}⁡(2t)),\\,-\\frac{3}{{t}^{2}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326895} {:answer/id #uuid "a337ebb4-d9cb-51bc-bece-a0805c6c2284" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4{sec}^{2}⁡(2t)(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t)),\\,-\\frac{3}{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326896} {:answer/id #uuid "15cae32f-f6af-53f8-b063-bb013b75ebd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t)({tan}^{2}⁡(2t)+{sec}^{2}⁡(2t)),\\,-\\frac{3}{{t}^{2}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326897} {:answer/id #uuid "973ba29b-5dbd-5622-8522-972a97c29bc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t)({tan}^{2}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t)),\\,\\frac{1}{{t}^{3}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326898}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15cae32f-f6af-53f8-b063-bb013b75ebd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t)({tan}^{2}⁡(2t)+{sec}^{2}⁡(2t)),\\,-\\frac{3}{{t}^{2}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326897} :answer-field/id #uuid "cecbaf67-2900-5422-ac5a-6e877bc6177d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326893}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b02b05ec-3c49-5ba7-a525-3faa0181bc7c" :question/math-academy-id "q-123184" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t),\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{3})⟩,$ ${r}^{″}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the second derivative of a vector-valued function, we find the second derivatives of the components.\n\n- For $x(t)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =2\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2t)\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t) \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =4\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t){tan}^{2}⁡(2t)+4\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t){sec}^{2}⁡(2t) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t)({tan}^{2}⁡(2t)+{sec}^{2}⁡(2t)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{3}),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{3}{t} \\\\ {y}^{″}(t) & =-\\frac{3}{{t}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨{x}^{″}(t),\\,{y}^{″}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t)({tan}^{2}⁡(2t)+{sec}^{2}⁡(2t)),\\,-\\frac{3}{{t}^{2}}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326899 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b31f2bdc-c267-5fc7-bd0f-283777ee4fee" :knowledge-point/title "The Derivative of a Three-Component Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aad541bc-d359-525b-ad4f-ea7ef1a14917" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,\\frac{1}{t+1},\\,2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326901} {:answer/id #uuid "0703f9f4-90d5-5b5e-9dff-1483f93aedfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,3{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326902} {:answer/id #uuid "f839a6b5-7a3a-5a25-ab36-a8f2f282d3c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{t+1},\\,3{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326903} {:answer/id #uuid "8e4259c0-424c-5584-bcc8-61aacfeb588f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,t+1,\\,{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326904} {:answer/id #uuid "5cc61d5f-e3ee-51db-aa9e-4b751a02d532" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{t+1},\\,2{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326905}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f839a6b5-7a3a-5a25-ab36-a8f2f282d3c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{t+1},\\,3{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326903} :answer-field/id #uuid "806b8b71-6909-5c2e-8646-470706062efd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326900}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "39f4772e-9bcf-5949-8e2e-5b11051dc7a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-130390" :question/problem "Calculate the derivative of  $f(t)=⟨\\frac{1}{t},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1),\\,{t}^{3}⟩$ with respect to $t.$" :question/worked-solution "We find the derivative of $f(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{t+1},\\,3{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326906 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b31f2bdc-c267-5fc7-bd0f-283777ee4fee" :knowledge-point/title "The Derivative of a Three-Component Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af21df73-b3d9-5292-8f71-844f46604c4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({e}^{t}+{sec}^{2}⁡t)\\,j+2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326908} {:answer/id #uuid "de380a5d-7be8-5bfa-9e9e-377458e79fe4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({e}^{t}+\\operatorname{sec}⁡t)\\,i+(2{t}^{2}+t)\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326909} {:answer/id #uuid "6a693f00-9cea-5f7c-812f-87f83dbbad5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({e}^{t}+{sec}^{2}⁡t)\\,i-2\\,j+(2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+t)\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326910} {:answer/id #uuid "4eeda593-52b3-5ae3-a94d-4d02bff9b1c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡t\\,i+(2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+t)\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326911} {:answer/id #uuid "0087253a-a7b9-5ed7-9742-ef999d49418f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({e}^{t}+{sec}^{2}⁡t)\\,i+(2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+t)\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326912}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0087253a-a7b9-5ed7-9742-ef999d49418f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({e}^{t}+{sec}^{2}⁡t)\\,i+(2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+t)\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326912} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ad567c9-78b9-5f1a-921f-cc2f5ea3642c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326907}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e39e9ea0-2d4a-5e70-a49b-0f623f92f7d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-130398" :question/problem "Find the derivative of  $f(t)=({e}^{t}+\\operatorname{tan}⁡t)\\,i-5\\,j+{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,k$ with respect to $t.$" :question/worked-solution "We find the derivative of $f(t)$  by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}+\\operatorname{tan}⁡t)\\,i-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)k \\\\  & =({e}^{t}+{sec}^{2}⁡t)\\,i-0\\,j+(2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+t)\\,k \\\\  & =({e}^{t}+{sec}^{2}⁡t)\\,i+(2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+t)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326913 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b31f2bdc-c267-5fc7-bd0f-283777ee4fee" :knowledge-point/title "The Derivative of a Three-Component Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c2d4f03-ab6e-5635-9b14-14ab3bc107dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{20}{{t}^{5}} \\\\ 2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ {2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326915} {:answer/id #uuid "c2d4415e-4f83-5e6c-86bb-48907f85f5aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{20}{{t}^{5}} \\\\ 2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ {2}^{t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326916} {:answer/id #uuid "a2cce6e9-d3cd-520f-ae9e-97a3f106bec8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{4{t}^{5}} \\\\ 2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ {2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326917} {:answer/id #uuid "af12dded-c617-51e9-bd8e-769b167d05c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{20}{{t}^{5}} \\\\ {t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ {2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326918} {:answer/id #uuid "77adfd15-d0f6-51dd-b6d1-a030ad811b06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{4{t}^{5}} \\\\ {t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326919}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c2d4f03-ab6e-5635-9b14-14ab3bc107dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{20}{{t}^{5}} \\\\ 2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ {2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326915} :answer-field/id #uuid "48243134-af2e-5187-86f1-80b407c2c68f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326914}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "422634d2-16ff-5174-a2f8-b71facc9ec9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-130400" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}^{′}(t)$ given that $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{{t}^{4}} \\\\ {t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ {2}^{t}\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "We find ${f}^{′}(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{5}{{t}^{4}}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({2}^{t})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{20}{{t}^{5}} \\\\ 2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ {2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326920 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b31f2bdc-c267-5fc7-bd0f-283777ee4fee" :knowledge-point/title "The Derivative of a Three-Component Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7eb633d4-0079-53a9-8172-5f1456794222" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}},\\,2(\\pi +2)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326922} {:answer/id #uuid "ee350e8f-e3a9-5f91-aa40-cf1327f9acc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}},\\,2(\\pi +2)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326923} {:answer/id #uuid "6f091b91-6def-5ea1-bde5-5fa47a8b54f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\pi ,\\,\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1},\\,2(2\\pi +1)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326924} {:answer/id #uuid "226f31a7-1245-552f-ac32-95475a41f3d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2\\pi ,\\,\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}},\\,2(\\pi -2)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326925} {:answer/id #uuid "05797936-01f2-5f56-b5c7-c67f343d824e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}},\\,2\\pi ⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326926}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee350e8f-e3a9-5f91-aa40-cf1327f9acc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}},\\,2(\\pi +2)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326923} :answer-field/id #uuid "8105f557-0b5d-57f1-a492-07d8920e63cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326921}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6d3b1235-338f-544b-9e5f-ca61081e2c9e" :question/math-academy-id "q-130408" :question/problem "Find the derivative of  $f(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1},\\,(t+2)^{2}⟩$ at $t=\\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((t+2)^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}},\\,2(t+2)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute ${f}^{′}(\\pi )$ we substitute $t=\\pi $ into the expression for ${f}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\pi ) & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\pi ,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}},\\,2(\\pi +2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}},\\,2(\\pi +2)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326927 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f0e2596-73d6-540c-af84-b19a943da6a8" :knowledge-point/title "The Second Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a515c34c-d77e-550c-a249-6eab2cf16e8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,i+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{e}^{t})\\,j+6t\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326929} {:answer/id #uuid "a5fe88e5-c2f4-50ad-846a-9df8a2f8256e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{t}\\,i-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{e}^{t})\\,j+2t\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326930} {:answer/id #uuid "6742b8d2-1aea-55a3-92df-7525a74715c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}\\,i-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{e}^{t})\\,j+2t+1\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326931} {:answer/id #uuid "7a01bbcf-71de-5010-9d8a-4f405dc4cf7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{t}^{2}\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+t\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326932} {:answer/id #uuid "7bbfc905-6a98-5370-8ddb-de8959594fc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}\\,i+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{e}^{t})\\,j+12t\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326933}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7bbfc905-6a98-5370-8ddb-de8959594fc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}\\,i+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{e}^{t})\\,j+12t\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326933} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1cf995c-6f1f-590f-985d-f3a61fcd8038" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326928}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "784dd9b4-e3bc-57ef-af5d-81abbd20ffed" :question/math-academy-id "q-130426" :question/problem "Find the second derivative of $f(t)=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,i-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{e}^{t})\\,j+(2{t}^{3}+t-2)\\,k$ with respect to $t.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the derivative of $f(t)$ by differentiating each component.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)\\,i-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{e}^{t})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3}+t-2)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{t}\\,i-(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{e}^{t})\\,j+(6{t}^{2}+1)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{t}\\,i+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-{e}^{t})\\,j+(6{t}^{2}+1)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThen, we calculate ${f}^{″}(t)$ by differentiating ${f}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2}{t})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-{e}^{t})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{t}^{2}+1)\\,k \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}\\,i+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{e}^{t})\\,j+12t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198870 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b31f2bdc-c267-5fc7-bd0f-283777ee4fee" :knowledge-point/title "The Derivative of a Three-Component Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8137a8ff-b68c-5072-bf40-cff9ad06083f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3t^{2} + 10t \\\\ \\sec^{2} t \\\\ 6^{t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197456} {:answer/id #uuid "95f6c6ca-8b95-5860-8bee-4d06fdc902ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3t^{2} + 10t \\\\ \\sec^{2} t \\\\ 6^{t}\\ln 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197457} {:answer/id #uuid "edb3be8b-3a96-5052-a676-0fd51e412c9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}t^{2} + 5t \\\\ \\sec^{2} t \\\\ 6^{t}\\ln 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197458} {:answer/id #uuid "43fe1132-8933-5074-b351-2af945d72ab4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3t^{2} + 10t \\\\ \\sec t \\\\ 6^{t}\\ln 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197459} {:answer/id #uuid "7b49052a-5bf2-5992-9e86-a07a5e369039" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3t^{2} + 10t \\\\ \\csc^{2} t \\\\ 6^{t}\\ln 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197460}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95f6c6ca-8b95-5860-8bee-4d06fdc902ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3t^{2} + 10t \\\\ \\sec^{2} t \\\\ 6^{t}\\ln 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197457} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c9ec6a6-0db9-5452-8f08-393cefaecc44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186197455}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "74e54a04-5388-5c59-b810-bdb93752e4b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-32415" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}^{′}(t)$ given that $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{3}+5{t}^{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ {6}^{t}\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "We find ${f}^{′}(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}+5{t}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({6}^{t})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3{t}^{2}+10t \\\\ {sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ {6}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326934 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f0e2596-73d6-540c-af84-b19a943da6a8" :knowledge-point/title "The Second Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b34f122b-944c-541e-a3fe-8f29d2c332c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s,12{s}^{2},1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326936} {:answer/id #uuid "916facc5-66a2-5d9b-b499-c237e8874eb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s,4{s}^{3}+10,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326937} {:answer/id #uuid "5f2a5a48-3ea8-5a19-8b03-b9dcb8e71071" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s,12{s}^{2},0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326938} {:answer/id #uuid "422d5ee2-0ed8-5f36-88c9-958090098c05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s,4{s}^{3}+10,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326939} {:answer/id #uuid "4c5a9c61-6049-57af-8213-6b509f491b64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s,12{s}^{2},0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326940}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f2a5a48-3ea8-5a19-8b03-b9dcb8e71071" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s,12{s}^{2},0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326938} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb3aa70a-d61d-5444-b63c-4c74ae92778d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326935}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "572464ad-7c54-5cd9-9015-36b55e4e1b81" :question/math-academy-id "q-32416" :question/problem "Calculate the second derivative of  $f(s)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s,\\,{s}^{4}+10s,\\,55⟩$ with respect to $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the derivative of $f(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}({s}^{4}+10s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(55)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s,\\,4{s}^{3}+10,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the second derivative by differentiating ${f}^{′}(s)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(4{s}^{3}+10),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s,\\,12{s}^{2},\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326941 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "072ad553-dd0b-58e0-b3e2-082c6d9866dd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6673f5f5-518f-515d-a011-7e4f467a67b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326943}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6673f5f5-518f-515d-a011-7e4f467a67b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3e^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326943} :answer-field/id #uuid "edca0f77-c72b-54f0-88eb-385166031536" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326942} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56ee9c24-baa8-540d-be2e-dcc2dddb01c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326945}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56ee9c24-baa8-540d-be2e-dcc2dddb01c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326945} :answer-field/id #uuid "65f326d8-0d4f-5a17-8877-2a0bbeacdc4c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326944}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5d77ce32-0cd3-5cc9-930e-2d996cff969e" :question/math-academy-id "q-347619" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨{e}^{3t}-4,\\,6\\sqrt{t}⟩,$ what is ${r}^{′}(t)?$\n\n${r}^{′}(t)=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)={e}^{3t}-4,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=3{e}^{3t}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=6\\sqrt{t},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=\\frac{6}{2\\sqrt{t}}=\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{e}^{3t},\\,\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326946 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "072ad553-dd0b-58e0-b3e2-082c6d9866dd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78bc53ad-0327-5610-8ddf-c5d25c189594" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326948} {:answer/id #uuid "319f4de3-4270-5152-a033-34aa45cd1a69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326949}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "319f4de3-4270-5152-a033-34aa45cd1a69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326949} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c566ab8-7080-51e1-8818-8c8bd6d599d0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326947} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "726da3c0-bab6-5518-a424-d15bd34f0bae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "726da3c0-bab6-5518-a424-d15bd34f0bae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326951} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9af2f6c-85f0-5b58-a303-10540c542ab4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326950}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3afbda33-c7c2-580e-b2cd-cf4f091a3552" :question/math-academy-id "q-349470" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨4+3{t}^{2},\\,4{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}-1⟩,$ what is ${r}^{′}(1)?$\n\n${r}^{′}(1)=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=4+3{t}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=6t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(1)=6\\cdot 1=6.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=4{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}-1,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=12{t}^{2}+6t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(1)=12\\cdot {1}^{2}+6\\cdot 1=18.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(1) & =⟨{x}^{′}(1),\\,{y}^{′}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,\\,18⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326952 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "072ad553-dd0b-58e0-b3e2-082c6d9866dd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f2cf53f-0a03-5492-badf-23567511c513" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{289}{8}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326954}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f2cf53f-0a03-5492-badf-23567511c513" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{289}{8}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326954} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d016461-d01f-5e87-b800-716e6141c9ae" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326953}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b3f67fdf-42e5-51a2-b0ea-ed2cd345e814" :question/math-academy-id "q-350217" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\sqrt{1-t},\\,3{t}^{2}⟩,$ what is $|{r}^{′}(-1)|?$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$|{r}^{′}(-1)|=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=\\sqrt{1-t},$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1-t}},\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(-1)=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1-(-1)}}=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=3{t}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=6t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(-1)=6(-1)=-6.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(-1) & =⟨{x}^{′}(-1),\\,{y}^{′}(-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}},\\,-6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, computing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{r}^{′}(-1)| & =\\sqrt{{(-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}})}^{2}+{(-6)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{8}+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{289}{8}} \\\\  & =\\frac{17\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186296337 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "072ad553-dd0b-58e0-b3e2-082c6d9866dd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5aff8bf9-2be5-5fea-9bca-d1ab4e8518e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,8{e}^{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296339} {:answer/id #uuid "a02992c9-bb0d-53e8-8eee-9ab879a36726" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,8{e}^{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296340} {:answer/id #uuid "5af4e518-15cd-5056-b76e-8979a49a9066" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,{e}^{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296341} {:answer/id #uuid "499b53ad-0f19-573e-9e6f-6c6b1e5c759d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296342} {:answer/id #uuid "7d81d374-3be8-5dad-bad8-7bbfcbcd0fd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296343}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5aff8bf9-2be5-5fea-9bca-d1ab4e8518e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,8{e}^{t}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296339} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe23e1b9-a6e4-5d5c-acb8-5f1d8899b18b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296338}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6eef8652-af24-51e5-8f51-46e17a486c11" :question/math-academy-id "q-50373" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}-1),\\,8{e}^{t}⟩,$ ${r}^{′}(t)=$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}-1),$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=8{e}^{t},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=8{e}^{t}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,8{e}^{t}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326955 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "072ad553-dd0b-58e0-b3e2-082c6d9866dd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a6a5dbe-8006-5c5c-8e74-c1d498ca7690" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,\\,\\sqrt{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326957} {:answer/id #uuid "7e1d9d6c-1b26-5894-b9af-9ee7af0c1927" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,\\,\\sqrt{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326958} {:answer/id #uuid "3b5d4141-4fbd-507e-8f20-929a4512ff2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,\\,\\sqrt{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326959} {:answer/id #uuid "d45aed39-10a1-5375-8ac8-b2db77e6d814" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}⟨2,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326960} {:answer/id #uuid "85ab4971-69c0-5674-8176-d80aec482697" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}⟨4,\\,\\frac{1}{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326961}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e1d9d6c-1b26-5894-b9af-9ee7af0c1927" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,\\,\\sqrt{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326958} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae9c124a-509d-5ffe-b4a1-bfc5adb2eecf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326956}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "18df67e9-e8a6-53fd-b815-f8c50e7fd68d" :question/math-academy-id "q-50411" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t⟩,$ ${r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=2{sec}^{2}⁡t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=2{sec}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=2{(\\sqrt{2})}^{2}=4.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 1=\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =⟨{x}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}),\\,{y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,\\sqrt{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326962 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f0e2596-73d6-540c-af84-b19a943da6a8" :knowledge-point/title "The Second Derivative of a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0da4a1bb-c19c-517d-8851-27a833d56cbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+(2t-1)\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326964} {:answer/id #uuid "84747db9-ea74-5cd7-9571-7acebd579dd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i-(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+(t+1)\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326965} {:answer/id #uuid "54dfd46e-f6be-5bcb-a8d2-cac0ff2ff613" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i-(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+(t+1)\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326966} {:answer/id #uuid "38bdc08f-34a7-5136-9a7f-9b4305f61b5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+(2t-1)\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326967} {:answer/id #uuid "3ef12aaa-afb9-5d01-8fca-0947ba2be086" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+(2t-1)\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326968}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38bdc08f-34a7-5136-9a7f-9b4305f61b5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+(2t-1)\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326967} :answer-field/id #uuid "049d0968-ff5d-5d86-b4a3-2982ba280e07" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326963}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "19d44fb9-0b26-5bc1-af60-efeec2020695" :question/math-academy-id "q-77683" :question/problem "Find the second derivative of $f(t)=t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+(\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2})\\,k$ with respect to $t.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the derivative of $f(t)$ by differentiating each component.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j+(3\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{t}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}t)\\,k \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j+({t}^{2}-t)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we calculate ${f}^{″}(t)$ by differentiating ${f}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-t)\\,k \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+(2t-1)\\,k \\\\  & =-(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+(2t-1)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
